From 40a3b4b1439628081325cb993000af3fd970ff79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anshul Noori <anshulnoori@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 23:38:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat: implement VK_EXT_depth_clip_enable

steamac: backport of KhronosGroup/MoltenVK PR #2712 (commit dc89e437,
https://github.com/KhronosGroup/MoltenVK/pull/2712) onto utmapp/MoltenVK
geometry-shaders 05604465 + the reversed-depth viewport backport.

Implementation (KosmicKrisp approach): clamp off/clip on -> Metal clip;
clamp on/clip off -> Metal clamp; both off -> Metal clamp + [0,1] viewport +
shader viewport-Z transform; both on -> Metal clip + fragment depth clamp.
Needs SPIRV-Cross emulate_depth_clip_enable (carried as a steamac
SPIRV-Cross patch).

Conflict resolution / deviations from the PR:
- no DrawId implicit buffer in the fork (needsDrawId dropped), keep needsXfbBuffer.
- Metal OpenGL-mode compensation dropped (mslOptions.use_opengl_mode does not
  exist in any published SPIRV-Cross; the viewport znear tweak needs it).
  canUseMetalOpenGLMode() still gates setOpenGLModeEnabled.
- keep the fork's fragment check_discarded_frag_stores logic.
- geometry-shader (object/mesh) stages: depth-clip and reversed-depth
  emulation forced off; the mesh path writes positions outside emit_fixup.
